%I A400130 #10 Sep 30 2026 15:44:53
%S A400130 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,28,670,16994,449040
%N A400130 Number of unlabeled connected planar simple graphs G on n vertices for which there exist a vertex v of degree 5 and a proper 4-coloring of G-v using all four colors on the neighbors of v such that no standard immediate Kempe repair succeeds.
%C A400130 The standard immediate repairs are single Kempe-chain interchanges and the two-interchange repair used in Kempe's coloring method.
%C A400130 The property holds if there exists a vertex v of degree 5 and a proper 4-coloring of G-v satisfying the stated condition. It is invariant under graph relabeling.
%C A400130 Terms are from exhaustive computation. The n=13 computation covered all 5942258308 connected planar graphs in 4096 shards with identical searcher and generator provenance.
%H A400130 E. Gethner et al., <a href="https://doi.org/10.2140/involve.2009.2.249">How False Is Kempe's Proof of the Four Color Theorem? Part II</a>, Involve 2 (2009), 249-265.
%H A400130 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KempeChain.html">Kempe Chain</a>.
%H A400130 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KempeImpasse.html">Kempe Impasse</a>.
%H A400130 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Kempe-KittellColoringAlgorithm.html">Kempe-Kittell Coloring Algorithm</a>.
%H A400130 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KempesColoringAlgorithm.html">Kempe's Coloring Algorithm</a>.
%H A400130 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PlanarConnectedGraph.html">Planar Connected Graph</a>.
%e A400130 a(9) = 2 since the Fritsch graph and Soifer graph are the two such graphs on 9 vertices.
%Y A400130 Cf. A003094 (all unlabeled connected planar simple graphs).
%Y A400130 Cf. A400129 (graphs with a four-color neighborhood before any repair is attempted).
